{"book":24,"chapter":22,"context":{"chapter":22,"title":"Woe to Unjust Kings","summary":"At the palace Jeremiah calls the king to justice or ruin. He judges three of Josiah's successors: Shallum will die in exile; Jehoiakim, who builds his palace with unpaid labor, will get a donkey's burial; and Coniah will be cast out, recorded as 'childless' as far as the throne is concerned.","background":"After Josiah died in 609 BC, his son Shallum (Jehoahaz) reigned three months before Pharaoh Neco took him to Egypt (2 Kings 23:31-34). Jehoiakim taxed the land to pay Egypt while building himself a lavish palace. Coniah (Jehoiachin) was taken to Babylon in 597 BC; Babylonian ration tablets later list oil allotted to 'Yaukin, king of Judah.'","customs":[{"term":"The signet upon my right hand","verses":"22:24","note":"A signet ring carried its owner's seal and authority and was never far from him. God would pull even this off. Haggai 2:23 reverses the image for Zerubbabel, Jehoiachin's grandson."}],"watchFor":["Josiah as the model: 'was not this to know me?' (v. 16).","'O earth, earth, earth' (v. 29).","'Write ye this man childless' (v. 30): he had sons (1 Chronicles 3:17), but none reigned."],"connections":["2 Kings 23:31-35","2 Kings 24:8-15","Haggai 2:23","1 Chronicles 3:17"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["כֹּה","koh","H3541","HD","thus"],["אָמַר","'amar","H559","HVqp3ms","he said"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["רֵד","red","H3381","HVqv2ms","go down"],["בֵּית","beit-","H1004","HNcmsc","[the] house of"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["וְדִבַּרְתָּ","vedibarta","H1696","Hc/Vpq2ms","and you will speak"],["שָׁם","sham","H8033","HD","there"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["הַדָּבָר","hadavar","H1697","HTd/Ncmsa","the word"],["הַזֶּה","hazeh","H2088","HTd/Tm","<the> this"]],"x":[[24034002,24034002,3]],"xn":1},"2":{"w":[["וְאָמַרְתָּ","ve'amarta","H559","Hc/Vqq2ms","and you will say"],["שְׁמַע","shem